# @trempel/kit — actions of this kit version for the Trempel hub

The hub (`@trempel/hub`, `trempel run <id>`) reads this file from the project's
`node_modules/@trempel/kit/hub/` — a project gets the dev server, builds, gates and the editor of
the kit it runs on. The project overrides any of them by id (`## actions` of `.trempel/project.mdz`).
Field reference — the hub's README.

## actions

### dev
$title: Dev server
$icon: play
$group: run
$pin: true
$kind: service
$port: auto
$shell: npx vite --port ${port} --strictPort

### build:web
$title: Build (web)
$icon: package
$group: build
$shell: npx vite build --mode web

### build:yt
$title: Build (YouTube Playables) + gates
$icon: package
$group: gates
$shell: npx vite build --mode youtube

The YouTube build runs the kit's Playables gates (size, sterility, metadata, services) and writes
`build-report.md`; a failed gate fails the action.

### test
$title: Unit tests
$icon: check
$group: gates
$pin: true
$shell: npx vitest run --passWithNoTests

### e2e
$title: e2e (web + YouTube builds, Playwright)
$icon: check
$group: gates
$when: file:playwright.config.ts
$shell: $[npx vite build --mode web, npx vite build --mode youtube, npx playwright test]

### editor
$title: Scene editor
$icon: edit
$group: run
$pin: true
$kind: service
$port: auto
$input.folder: { type: "text", default: "scenes", label: "Scenes folder" }
$when: file:${pkg:@trempel/scene}/edit/cli.mjs
$shell: node ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/edit/cli.mjs ${input.folder} --port ${port}

The editor page of the scene package this kit runs with (`<folder>/trempel.view.ts` plugs the
kit's inspectors in). While it runs, `editor:eval` / `editor:save` / `editor:state` reach the open
page through its agent bridge (`trempel-edit`).

### editor:eval
$title: Editor: run a script
$icon: terminal
$group: agents
$when: running:editor
$input.code: { type: "text", label: "tml script (edit/API.md)" }
$shell: node ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/view/edit-bin.mjs eval --port ${services.editor.port} ${input.code}

### editor:save
$title: Editor: save (⌘S)
$icon: save
$group: agents
$when: running:editor
$shell: node ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/view/edit-bin.mjs save --port ${services.editor.port}

### editor:state
$title: Editor: state
$icon: info
$group: agents
$when: running:editor
$shell: node ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/view/edit-bin.mjs state --port ${services.editor.port}

### editor:mcp
$title: Editor: MCP server line for an agent
$icon: robot
$group: agents
$when: running:editor
$shell: node -e "console.log(JSON.stringify({ command: 'node', args: [process.argv[1], 'mcp', '--port', process.argv[2]] }, null, 2))" ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/view/edit-bin.mjs ${services.editor.port}

Prints the MCP server entry (stdio) of the running editor's bridge — `editor.eval`, `editor.save`,
`editor.state` — to paste into an agent's MCP config.

### view:shot
$title: Scene snapshot (PNG)
$icon: camera
$group: content
$input.scene: { type: "file", label: "Scene (X.svg / X.tml.svg)" }
$input.out: { type: "text", default: "shot.png" }
$input.settle: { type: "text", default: 2, label: "Seconds after mount" }
$shell: node ${pkg:@trempel/scene}/view/bin.mjs view:shot ${input.scene} --out ${input.out} --settle ${input.settle}
